\title{Count lines in a \code{\verb~|Text~} with fixed vectors}
\taxon{Example}
\date{2026-11-13}
\author{claude-fable-5-2}
\contributor{schrodingerzy}
\tag{simd}
\tag{example}
\import{base-macros}

\p{A count over 32-byte chunks. Each chunk yields a mask, and the number of set lanes is added to a scalar. A \code{\verb~|Text~} is either a literal or an owned string; its data pointer hides the difference.}
\pre{\verb~|
import core::ptr;
import core::simd;
import core::ptr::PtrArithFlag;
import std::text::Text;

pub fn lines(t: Text) -> u64 {
    let len = t.len();
    core::object::unsafe_inc(t);
    let base = t.unsafe_data_ptr();
    let newline = simd::splat<Simd<[u8; 32]>>(10);
    let zero = simd::splat<Simd<[u8; 32]>>(0);
    let (end, total) = while [i = 0, total = 0] (i < len) {
        let live = simd::mask_first<Simd<[bool; 32]>>(len - i);
        let chunk = simd::load<Simd<[u8; 32]>>(
            ptr::offset(base, i as i64, PtrArithFlag::Inbounds), live, zero);
        (i + 32, total + simd::count(simd::eq(chunk, newline, live)))
    };
    core::object::unsafe_dec(t);
    total
}
~}
\ul{
\li{The same source works with \code{\verb~|Simd<[u8; [16]]>~} and a step of \code{\verb~|lanes~}; the fixed form is shown because a fixed vector may also be kept in a record, for example as a precomputed table.}
\li{A faster variant keeps a vector of per-lane counters and reduces it once at the end; it needs a flush every 255 iterations when the counters are bytes.}
}
\p{Belongs to [SIMD vectors](design-simd-vectors). Written against the draft; not compiled.}
